# Sub-tick interpolation of the cyclorama (scripts/check_feeder_subtick.sh
# --path cyclorama).
#   <bk2> | <V> | blob=<x>,<y> ... [tol=<px>] [step=<px>] [atol=<px>] [ctol=<n>]
# V is the tick whose primitives the intermediate present at V+1 replays; V-2
# opens the interval that present covers.
#
# The cyclorama has no feed knob, so the two legs are a render-path selection
# with and without it, terrain in both: the horizon the cyclorama is seen
# against is then identical between them and the difference holds the sky
# alone.
#
# The cyclorama is a 360-degree surround whose texture the camera's yaw scrolls
# across the frame; a row therefore needs a turning camera, not a moving one.
# At V=1350 of this same movie the camera holds its heading and the whole
# 241676-px sky mask displaces 0.4 px over the interval, below every floor. At
# V=852 the camera swings through the portal entry and the cloud the row names
# crosses 26 px.
autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry.bk2 | 852 | blob=82.2,38.0 tol=1.0 step=10
